# propranolol.msf
# Propranolol  pKa=9.530 (isopropylammonium→amine, q=+1→0)
# Source: Avdeef 2001
# Beta-blocker. Secondary amine (NH-iPr) at pKa=9.53: at pH 7.4, >99%
# protonated → highly water-soluble. The naphthyloxy group creates unique
# ΔBO_ring relative to simple aliphatic amines (BO change propagates into
# naphthalene on deprotonation via C-O-C conjugation). Historically one
# of the first examples where pKa-lipophilicity relationships were derived.

